Metropolis-Hastings

Metropolis-Hastings algorithm


Choose an initial value for a sample x_{0}
Propose a new sample value x_{i+1} given x_{i} from q(x\mid x_{i})
Compute the probability of accepting a new parameter value by using the Metropolis-Hastings criteria: \begin{equation}
\rho=\min\left(1,\frac{p(x_{i+1})}{p(x_{i})}\right)
\end{equation}
Sample u from a \mathcal{U}[0,1]
If u&lt;\rho we accept the new value x_{i+1}; otherwise, we stay in the old value x_{i}




